-- title:
--   Chart-ideal membership on D₊(xᵢ) versus xᵢ^N F ∈ I
-- statement:
--   Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$, a commutative ring $A$, an arbitrary ideal $I$ of the polynomial ring $S = A[x_0,\dots,x_n] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) A` (graded by the submodules of homogeneous elements), an index $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$, a natural number $d$, and $F \in S$ homogeneous of degree $d$. Write $\varphi$ for the canonical ring map `Proj.awayToSection` from the degree-zero part $S^0_{(x_i)}$ of the localisation of $S$ at $x_i$ into the sections of the structure sheaf of $\operatorname{Proj} S$ over the basic open set $D_+(x_i)$, and for homogeneous $G$ of degree $e$ let $[G/x_i^e]$ denote the class in $S^0_{(x_i)}$ with numerator $G$, denominator $x_i^e$ (a power of $x_i$) and degree $e$. The assertion is that $\varphi([F/x_i^d])$ lies in the ideal of $\Gamma(D_+(x_i), \mathcal{O})$ generated by all $\varphi([G/x_i^e])$ with $e \in \mathbb{N}$ and $G \in I$ homogeneous of degree $e$, if and only if $x_i^N F \in I$ for some $N \in \mathbb{N}$. No homogeneity hypothesis on $I$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the standard dictionary between an ideal of a graded polynomial ring and the ideal it generates on an affine chart $D_+(x_i)$ of projective space, saturation by $x_i$ being the kernel of the comparison. It is used in the identification of ideals cutting out closed subschemes of $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ chart by chart, in particular by [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.eq_ker_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.eq_ker_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion) and in the Hilbert-functor representability statements that rest on it.
